course: dictionary
lesson: 1387
title: Captions: words that explain pictures
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A caption is a short piece of writing next to a picture, photo or cartoon. It tells you what the picture shows or why it matters. «Newspaper features include a headline, a photo, a caption and columns.» Here the caption sits beside the photo and helps you understand it.
explain: Captions can also be words shown on a screen that write down what people say. These help people who cannot hear well follow a film or video. «Automatic captions guess words from sound and sometimes mishear, which matters a lot for deaf viewers.» So a caption is only as good as the guess behind it.
explain: To caption a picture means to write a caption for it. You might caption your own diagram in a science project. Always ask yourself: does this caption really match the picture?
fact: A caption is a short piece of text next to a picture, photo or cartoon that explains it.
fact: Captions are a feature of information texts, such as diagrams and posters.
fact: Closed captions or subtitles write down what people say, so deaf viewers can follow.
fact: Captions can be misleading, so always check where a picture came from.
fact: «Cropping a photo can make a crowd look huge or tiny», so a caption can change how we see a picture.
exercise: «A caption is a short piece of text next to a picture.» What is a caption? | A sound played during a video | A long story that replaces the picture | A kind of camera | *A short piece of text that explains a picture
exercise: «Closed captions help deaf viewers follow what people say.» What do captions on a screen do? | *Write down what people say | Make the picture brighter | Turn the screen off | Play music more loudly
exercise: «Mia will caption her drawing of the volcano.» Find and copy the word that means to write a caption. | drawing | Mia | volcano | *caption
test: «Old videos are sometimes shared with new captions as if they were happening now; this is recycled footage.» Why should you check a picture's caption? | Because captions only appear on films | Because captions are always true | *Because captions can mislead, so check where the picture came from | Because captions make pictures smaller
test: «A meme is a funny picture or video with words, called a caption, that gets copied and shared.» Can a meme's caption explain a whole story? | Yes, every meme explains a whole story | Yes, but only if it is very long | Only in a newspaper | *No, a meme cannot explain a whole story
exam: Jayden says captions are always true because they are written under a photo. What should you tell him? | Yes, captions are always true | Captions only work on films, so they don't matter for photos | Captions are the same thing as the picture | *Captions can be misleading, so check where the picture came from
